---
// /benchmark/: how well each harness + provider + model does the tracker's own research job,
// measured on real pages with known answers (benchmark/README.md).
import Base from "../../src/layouts/Base.astro";
import "./benchmark.css";
import { runs, cases, sets, FAMILIES, FAMILY_NOTE, CAPABILITIES, day, score, band } from "./data.js";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const { full, partial } = sets();
const current = full[0];
const older = full.slice(1);
const families = Object.keys(FAMILIES);
const caps = Object.keys(CAPABILITIES);
const weights = runs[0]?.weights ?? { facts: 20, figures: 20, classification: 10, corroboration: 15, photos: 10, text: 15, grounding: 10 };
const byFamily = families.map((family) => [family, cases.filter((item) => item.family === family)]);
const repeats = (run) => Math.max(1, Math.round(run.summary.attempts / Math.max(1, run.summary.cases)));
const caseScore = (run, id) => run.cases.find((item) => item.id === id)?.score;
const subjectLine = (run) => `${run.subject.harness}${run.subject.harness_version ? ` ${run.subject.harness_version.replace(/^\D+/, "")}` : ""} · ${run.subject.provider}`;
// short column titles for the wide table; the full names are the tooltips and the legend under it
const SHORT = { "new-event": "New", "known-event": "Known", "out-of-scope": "Scope", recognised: "Found", facts: "Facts", figures: "Figures", classification: "Class.", corroboration: "Sources", photos: "Photos", text: "Text", grounding: "Quotes" };
const modelName = (run) => run.subject.model + (run.subject.effort ? `#${run.subject.effort}` : "");
---
<Base title="Research benchmark" description="How well each AI model, with its harness and provider, does the tracker's research: recognising events, corroborating them, finding photos, getting figures and classification right." wide noindex>
  <div class="bench">
    <h1>Research benchmark</h1>
    <p class="lead">Which model can be trusted with the tracker's research? Each one gets the same {cases.length} real pages
      and does the whole job the way it runs in production: read the page, search for other coverage, check what the
      tracker already has, decide, and write the report. The result is compared with a checked answer.</p>

    <dl class="b-facts">
      <div><dt>Cases</dt><dd>{cases.length}</dd></div>
      {byFamily.map(([family, list]) => <div><dt>{FAMILIES[family]}</dt><dd>{list.length}</dd></div>)}
      <div><dt>Runs recorded</dt><dd>{runs.length}</dd></div>
    </dl>

    {!runs.length && (
      <p class="note">No run has been recorded yet. Start one with <code>npm run benchmark -- opencode@provider/model#effort</code>.</p>
    )}

    {current && (
      <>
        <h2 id="results">Results</h2>
        <p class="note">Scores are out of 100. A subject is always three things: the harness that drives the model, the
          provider that serves it, and the model with its effort setting. Change any of them and it is a different row.</p>
        <div class="b-scroll">
          <table class="b-table b-board">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th></th><th>Model</th><th class="n">Score</th>
                {families.map((family, i) => <th class:list={["n", { sep: i === 0 }]} title={`${FAMILIES[family]}: ${FAMILY_NOTE[family]}`}>{SHORT[family]}</th>)}
                {caps.map((cap, i) => <th class:list={["n", { sep: i === 0 }]} title={`${CAPABILITIES[cap][0]}: ${CAPABILITIES[cap][1]}`}>{SHORT[cap]}</th>)}
                <th class="n sep" title="Typical minutes for one case, from opening the page to the final answer">Min</th>
                <th class="n">Runs</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {current.runs.map((run, i) => (
                <tr>
                  <td class="rank">{i + 1}</td>
                  <td>
                    <span class="b-model"><a href={`${base}benchmark/${run.id}/`}>{modelName(run)}</a></span>
                    <span class="b-sub">{subjectLine(run)} · {day(run.started_at)}{run.label ? ` · ${run.label}` : ""}{run.complete ? "" : " · unfinished"}</span>
                  </td>
                  <td class="n"><span class:list={["b-total", `b-${band(run.summary.score)}`]}>{score(run.summary.score)}</span><span class="b-bar"><i style={`width:${run.summary.score ?? 0}%`}></i></span></td>
                  {families.map((family, j) => <td class:list={["n", { sep: j === 0 }, `b-${band(run.summary.families[family]?.score)}`]}>{score(run.summary.families[family]?.score)}</td>)}
                  {caps.map((cap, j) => <td class:list={["n", { sep: j === 0 }, `b-${band(run.summary.capabilities[cap]?.score)}`]}>{score(run.summary.capabilities[cap]?.score)}</td>)}
                  <td class="n sep">{run.summary.usage.minutes_per_case ?? "–"}</td>
                  <td class="n">{run.summary.cases}×{repeats(run)}{run.summary.verdicts.error ? <span class="b-sub b-fail">{run.summary.verdicts.error} unfinished</span> : ""}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="note"><b>New</b>, <b>Known</b>, <b>Scope</b>: the three kinds of case (new events, events already covered,
          pages out of scope). The next eight look inside the reports written for new events: <b>Found</b> (recognised as an
          event), <b>Facts</b>, <b>Figures</b>, <b>Class.</b> (classification), <b>Sources</b> (corroboration), <b>Photos</b>,
          <b>Text</b>, <b>Quotes</b> (grounding). <b>Min</b>: typical minutes per case. Open a model for every case in detail.</p>

        <h2 id="cases">Case by case</h2>
        <p class="note">Each cell is one model's score on one case (the mean, when a case was run several times).</p>
        <div class="b-scroll">
          <table class="b-table b-matrix">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Case</th>
                {current.runs.map((run) => <th class="col"><a href={`${base}benchmark/${run.id}/`}>{modelName(run)}<br /><span class="b-none">{subjectLine(run)}</span></a></th>)}
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {byFamily.map(([family, list]) => (
                <>
                  <tr class="fam"><td colspan={current.runs.length + 1}>{FAMILIES[family]} · {list.length}</td></tr>
                  {list.map((item) => (
                    <tr>
                      <td>
                        <span class="b-case-title">{item.title}</span>
                        <span class="b-case-id">{item.id}</span>
                        <span class="b-tests">{(item.tests || []).map((t) => <span>{t}</span>)}</span>
                      </td>
                      {current.runs.map((run) => {
                        const value = caseScore(run, item.id);
                        return <td class="cell">{value === undefined ? <span class="b-none">·</span> : <a class={`b-${band(value)}`} href={`${base}benchmark/${run.id}/#${item.id}`}>{score(value)}</a>}</td>;
                      })}
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </>
    )}

    {(older.length > 0 || partial.length > 0) && (
      <>
        <h2 id="other">Other runs</h2>
        <p class="note">Runs on an earlier set of cases, other run settings or older scoring rules, and runs of only some
          cases. They are kept for reference and are not ranked against the table above.</p>
        <div class="b-scroll">
          <table class="b-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th class="n">Score</th><th class="n">Cases</th><th>Why apart</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {[...older.flatMap((set) => set.runs.map((run) => [run, "earlier cases, settings or rules"])), ...partial.map((run) => [run, run.full_set ? "stopped before the end" : "only some cases"])].map(([run, reason]) => (
                <tr>
                  <td><span class="b-model"><a href={`${base}benchmark/${run.id}/`}>{modelName(run)}</a></span><span class="b-sub">{subjectLine(run)} · {day(run.started_at)}</span></td>
                  <td class:list={["n", `b-${band(run.summary.score)}`]}>{score(run.summary.score)}</td>
                  <td class="n">{run.summary.cases}×{repeats(run)}</td>
                  <td>{reason}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </>
    )}

    <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A run starts a private copy of the tracker's own research service, the same program and the same instructions
        that research submissions in production, with the model under test. It works against a copy of the reports in
        which the answers to the cases have been taken out. Each case's page is submitted like any link a reader sends.
        Nothing is published: the copy is thrown away after the run. The live tracker already shows the hidden
        answers, so in the copy the model is told that the tracker's own site is never a source; an answer that
        names a hidden report anyway is marked spoiled and not counted.</p>
      <p>What the service ends with is then compared, by fixed rules and without a judging model, with an answer that was
        checked by hand against the sources.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Three kinds of case</h3>
    <div class="b-scroll">
      <table class="b-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th class="n">Cases</th><th>What is asked</th><th>How it is scored</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>{FAMILIES["new-event"]}</td><td class="n">{byFamily[0][1].length}</td><td>{FAMILY_NOTE["new-event"]}</td><td>No report: 0. Otherwise the report is scored part by part (below).</td></tr>
          <tr><td>{FAMILIES["known-event"]}</td><td class="n">{byFamily[1][1].length}</td><td>{FAMILY_NOTE["known-event"]}</td><td>100 when it is attached to the right report or called its duplicate; 0 for a second report or the wrong one.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>{FAMILIES["out-of-scope"]}</td><td class="n">{byFamily[2][1].length}</td><td>{FAMILY_NOTE["out-of-scope"]}</td><td>100 for the right decision, part credit for another rejection, 0 for a report.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>Inside a report</h3>
    <div class="b-scroll">
      <table class="b-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Part</th><th class="n">Weight</th><th>What is checked</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {Object.keys(weights).map((key) => <tr><td>{CAPABILITIES[key][0]}</td><td class="n">{weights[key]}</td><td>{CAPABILITIES[key][1]}</td></tr>)}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>A part that a case cannot test is left out for that case: a story only one outlet carried has no corroboration
        score. Many cases hold a trap that halves the figures score when it is walked into, such as pounds recorded as
        kilograms or cocaine added to the cannabis weight.</p>
      <p>The overall score is the mean over all cases. Models differ from run to run, so a difference of a few points
        between two rows means little; repeat a run (<code>--repeat 3</code>) to see how much one model varies.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Running it</h3>
    <pre><code>npm run benchmark -- opencode@swancloud/muse-spark-1.3-contributor#xhigh
npm run benchmark -- muse@muse-spark-1.3#xhigh --repeat 3
npm run benchmark:scores</code></pre>
    <p class="note">The cases, the scoring rules and every run's full output are in the repository's <code>benchmark/</code> folder.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
